// =====================================================================
// /app/briefs/create-brief — v4 MULTI-SOURCE create chat.
//
// Lee walks the user from workspace to a created brief in one thread:
//
//   1. Workspace  — the user's own accounts, scoped IN THE QUERY
//                   (users .is current user). One auto-selects; several
//                   show a picker. ?workspace=<accountId> (written by
//                   /settings/workspace-switcher) wins over both.
//   1b. PDF       — "Already have this brief written?" Upload a PDF
//                   (useUpload), OpenRouter reads it in the writing
//                   call itself (file content part + the free
//                   cloudflare-ai parser plugin; base64 under 4MB,
//                   the hosted URL for larger files) and maps it
//                   VERBATIM into the section fields. The original file can
//                   attach to the brief (attachment dgOkq). The
//                   product step is skipped on this path.
//   2. Project    — projects inside that workspace. REQUIRED: every
//                   brief is created WITH its project linked, there is
//                   no skip. A workspace with no projects gets sent to
//                   create one first. When the modal URL already
//                   carries ?recordId=<projectId> (opened from a
//                   project page) this step is skipped.
//   3. Product    — pick from the workspace catalog, paste a URL
//                   (Firecrawl reads the page once and a products row
//                   is written, so the catalog builds itself), or
//                   "no product" for brand or organic content.
//   4. Basics     — name, creator type, channel, optional goal.
//   5. Write      — "Write it with AI" calls OpenRouter in THREE
//                   parallel calls, prose + lists + visual format
//                   (one call writing all 11 sections ran V4 Pro past
//                   the ~120s proxy limit), V4 Pro first, V4 Flash
//                   retry per call, and fills the per-section
//                   HTML fields, same keys as create-brief-quick's
//                   section model. The format leg picks two or three
//                   from the 42-format library and writes the creator
//                   direction for each; a name the library does not
//                   hold is dropped rather than written, so the model
//                   cannot invent a format. A failed write still
//                   creates the brief so nothing is lost, and a failed
//                   format leg leaves the other two untouched. The PDF
//                   route picks its formats from what it extracted,
//                   not from the file, because the mapper is told to
//                   pull verbatim and never invent. "Open the builder"
//                   saves the answers without writing. Both land in
//                   /briefs/details.
//
// MULTI-SOURCE: six sources are wired, so EVERY hook names its source
// via `from`. The ids below are this block's own connection ids from
// the Source tab (they differ per block for the same table).
//
// SOFTR CONFIG:
//   Source tab: briefs + accounts + products + projects + Firecrawl
//   + OpenRouter (all wired 2026-08-26). Visibility: logged-in users.
//   Actions: ADD_RECORD (briefs, products) registers itself from the
//   aliases in createFields / productCreate on compile. The briefs
//   write list grew by three on the visual-format change (format,
//   first_format, visual_format), so re-sync the Actions tab after
//   pasting. A recompile also resets action VISIBILITY to defaults,
//   so re-check BOTH actions after every push.
// =====================================================================

